%SIXMD 1
# @?INSTALL - COPY FILES WITH INSTALLATION PERMISSIONS

## DESCRIPTION

INSTALL COPIES A 36-BIT WORD STREAM INTO ITS DESTINATION AND SETS ITS MODE.
IT DOES NOT REINTERPRET S6REC TEXT OR DXR EXECUTABLE WORDS.

USAGE IS 'INSTALL [-M OCTAL-MODE] SOURCE DESTINATION'.

THE DEFAULT FILE MODE IS 0555. THE DESTINATION IS CREATED OR TRUNCATED.

INSTALL -D [-M OCTAL-MODE] DIRECTORY CREATES A DIRECTORY, IF IT DOES NOT
EXIST, AND SETS ITS MODE. PARENT DIRECTORIES MUST EXIST.

EXAMPLES:

    INSTALL -D -M 0755 /OPTION/BASE/LIBEXEC/KCC
    INSTALL -M 0555 KCC.DXR /OPTION/BASE/EXEC/KCC

INSTALL RETURNS ZERO ON SUCCESS AND ONE ON FAILURE. SOURCE AND DESTINATION
MUST REFER TO DIFFERENT FILES.
